---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Fantasy Football World Cup — Draft & Simulate | World Cup Simulator"
  description="Build your fantasy World Cup dream team from 100+ historical squads (1970-2026), then watch them face the all-time greats in a simulated knockout tournament. Free browser game, no download."
>
  <main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas text-white">
    <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
      <div
        class="pointer-events-none absolute -top-48 left-1/2 h-96 w-2xl -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full bg-mint/15 blur-[120px]"
      >
      </div>
      <div
        class="pointer-events-none absolute top-24 -left-32 h-64 w-64 rounded-full bg-uv/20 blur-[100px]"
      >
      </div>

      <div
        class="relative mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 pt-16 pb-12 text-center sm:px-6 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-16"
      >
        <p
          class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase"
        >
          World Cup Draft Simulator
        </p>
        <h1
          class="mt-4 font-display text-6xl leading-[0.85] tracking-[1.07px] text-balance text-mint sm:text-7xl md:text-8xl"
        >
          Fantasy Football World Cup: Simulate the World Cup
        </h1>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-secondary">
          World Cup Draft Simulator is a free browser soccer game. It is a
          fantasy football world cup game. You draft a dream team from 100+ old
          World Cup squads. Pick Brazil 1970, France 1998 or Argentina 2022.
          Then the game simulates a full tournament for you. You get group
          games, a knockout bracket and penalty shootouts. It is a soccer
          simulator and a football draft simulator. You play it online. No
          download. No sign-up. In the US, people call it a soccer draft game or
          online soccer game. It is also a free soccer simulation game. The
          world cup simulator 2026 mode adds new squads. You can predict your
          own tournament today. Pick a formation, build your squad, and watch
          the cup.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
          <a
            href="/game"
            class="rounded-full bg-mint px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-black uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:bg-white"
          >
            Play Now
          </a>
          <a
            href="/how-to-play"
            class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-white uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:border-mint hover:text-mint"
          >
            How to play
          </a>
        </div>

        <ul class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-2">
          {
            [
              "1970-2026",
              "100+ squads",
              "12 draft rounds",
              "Group → knockout",
              "Penalty shootouts",
            ].map((s) => (
              <li class="rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-slate/40 px-4 py-1.5 font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-[1.5px] text-secondary uppercase">
                {s}
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-white/10 bg-slate/20">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
        <p
          class="text-center font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase"
        >
          How it works
        </p>
        <h2
          class="mt-3 text-center font-display text-4xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[0.5px] sm:text-5xl"
        >
          Four rounds to glory
        </h2>
        <ol class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
          <li
            class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate/40 p-5"
          >
            <span class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span
                class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-[1.5px] text-mint"
                >01</span
              >
            </span>
            <span class="mt-4 block font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px]"
              >Pick your shape</span
            >
            <span class="mt-2 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-secondary">
              Choose from 4-3-3, 4-4-2, 3-5-2 or 4-2-3-1. This locks the slot
              limits for all 12 draft rounds.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li
            class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate/40 p-5"
          >
            <span class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span
                class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-[1.5px] text-mint"
                >02</span
              >
            </span>
            <span class="mt-4 block font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px]"
              >Draft your XI</span
            >
            <span class="mt-2 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-secondary">
              Twelve rounds of picks from 100+ historical World Cup squads.
              Chase stars, patch gaps, keep one on the bench.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li
            class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate/40 p-5"
          >
            <span class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span
                class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-[1.5px] text-mint"
                >03</span
              >
            </span>
            <span class="mt-4 block font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px]"
              >Auto-run the cup</span
            >
            <span class="mt-2 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-secondary">
              Your tournament simulates itself — group stage, knockout bracket,
              extra time and penalty shootouts.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li
            class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate/40 p-5"
          >
            <span class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span
                class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-[1.5px] text-mint"
                >04</span
              >
            </span>
            <span class="mt-4 block font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px]"
              >Replay &amp; results</span
            >
            <span class="mt-2 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-secondary">
              Rewatch goals, compare squad stats, and lift the trophy when it's
              all over.
            </span>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div
          class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary"
        >
          <p>
            World Cup Draft Simulator is a fantasy football world cup game. It
            is easy to replay. The game has one simple loop.
          </p>
          <p>
            First, you pick your formation. You can pick 4-3-3 for attack. Or
            4-4-2 for balance. Or 3-5-2 for the midfield. Or 4-2-3-1 for
            control. Your choice locks the slots. You must fill them over 12
            draft rounds.
          </p>
          <p>
            Next, the football draft simulator shows you squads. These are old
            World Cup teams from 1970 to 2026. You build your dream XI one pick
            at a time. You chase the best players. You fill the gaps. You keep
            one player on the bench.
          </p>
          <p>
            When your squad is ready, the soccer simulator takes over. Your team
            joins a group with three AI teams. The match engine plays each group
            game. It shows possession, shots and chances. The knockout bracket
            runs by itself. You get the round of 16, the quarter-final, the
            semi-final and the final.
          </p>
          <p>
            Ties go to extra time. Then a penalty shootout simulator decides the
            winner. Each side takes five kicks. After that, it is sudden death.
            No two runs are the same. A Brazil 1970 attack can lose to a strong
            Germany 2014 defence. A weak draft can beat the top seeds.
          </p>
          <p>
            Players call it a soccer draft game and a world cup predictor. You
            are not predicting real results. You are predicting your own cup.
            When the final ends, you can replay any match. You can compare squad
            stats and player ratings. Then you can start a new draft.
          </p>
          <p>
            It is a free soccer simulation game. It runs in the browser. No
            download. No sign-up. It is an easy online soccer game for your
            phone. It is an interactive soccer simulator and a fantasy soccer
            draft. It is the world cup fantasy game. The steps never change:
            shape, draft, simulate, repeat.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-white/10">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
        <p
          class="text-center font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase"
        >
          The squads
        </p>
        <h2
          class="mt-3 text-center font-display text-4xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[0.5px] sm:text-5xl"
        >
          Every World Cup great, one pool
        </h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-center text-secondary">
          Draft from the semifinalists of every World Cup from 1970 to 2026.
          Browse the full squad pages with player ratings, then take them into
          the draft.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
          <a
            href="/teams"
            class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-white uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:border-mint hover:text-mint"
          >
            Browse all squads
          </a>
          <a
            href="/game"
            class="rounded-full bg-mint px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-black uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:bg-white"
          >
            Play now
          </a>
        </div>

        <div
          class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary"
        >
          <p>
            The squads are the heart of World Cup Draft Simulator. They make
            this football simulator special. Every team is a real World Cup
            semifinalist from 1970 to 2026. All teams use the same rating scale.
            So your draft and the AI teams are fair.
          </p>
          <p>
            The world cup winners, top scorers and best players are all here.
            You can pick them. Brazil 1970 was a great attacking team.
            Netherlands 1974 played total football. Argentina 1978 was strong.
            Italy 1982 was tough. France 1982 had skill. West Germany ruled the
            1980s. Argentina 1986 had Maradona. Italy 1990 was solid. Brazil
            1994 won. France 1998 had Zidane. Brazil 2002 had the three R's.
            Germany 2002 was good. Italy 2006 was defence. Spain 2010 played
            tiki-taka. Germany 2014 was a machine. France 2018 was young.
            Argentina 2022 had Messi.
          </p>
          <p>
            Each squad has player ratings. The ratings cover reflexes, tackling,
            passing, finishing, pace and vision. The ratings drive the world cup
            simulation. Draft players from the same nation. They get a chemistry
            boost. This helps your team. You can build the best world cup team
            of all time. Stack Brazil 1970 or Argentina 2022. The engine sees
            the bond.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can browse every roster first. Check the average rating. Find
            the best player. Then take that into the soccer draft game. The app
            is like a museum of greatest world cup teams. You put them on the
            pitch. Pit Maradona's Argentina against Messi's. Or Brazil 1970
            against France 2022. It all happens inside the simulator.
          </p>
          <p>
            The 2026 rosters are predicted. They are not official. The ratings
            are for balance, not facts. This keeps the fantasy soccer draft
            honest. The matches stay close. The squad pool is why this is a
            world cup fantasy game worth playing again. There is always one more
            great player to build around.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-white/10">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
        <p
          class="text-center font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase"
        >
          How to play
        </p>
        <h2
          class="mt-3 text-center font-display text-4xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[0.5px] sm:text-5xl"
        >
          Your world cup simulator, step by step
        </h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-center text-secondary">
          World Cup Draft Simulator is an interactive soccer simulator that
          turns drafting into a full tournament. Choose a formation, draft your
          dream XI from 100+ historical squads, then watch the engine simulate
          every match — group stage, knockout bracket, extra time and penalty
          shootouts — and predict your own cup. It's a free soccer simulation
          game you can play right in the browser, on any device.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
          <a
            href="/how-to-play"
            class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-white uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:border-mint hover:text-mint"
          >
            Full guide
          </a>
          <a
            href="/game"
            class="rounded-full bg-mint px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-black uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:bg-white"
          >
            Start drafting
          </a>
        </div>

        <div
          class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary"
        >
          <p>
            Your world cup simulator is easy to start. That is the point of an
            online soccer game in the browser. Open the app. One click and you
            can draft. No install. No account. No waiting.
          </p>
          <p>
            First, pick your formation. The soccer simulator respects positions.
            Your shape decides how many defenders, midfielders and attackers you
            take. You pick over 12 rounds. Then the football draft simulator
            shows offers. Each offer is a nation and a year. Brazil 1970 one
            pick. Germany 2014 the next. You place each player in the best slot.
            You watch chemistry update. You get a few rerolls if the board is
            bad.
          </p>
          <p>
            When your XI is done, the match engine simulates the group stage. It
            plays live, part by part. The rest of the bracket is pre-simulated.
            So the whole world cup simulation ends fast. Knockout ties go to
            extra time. Then a penalty shootout simulator decides. Five kicks
            each. Then sudden death. This is the drama fans love.
          </p>
          <p>
            You are not predicting real 2026 results. You use the world cup
            simulator 2026 mode to predict your own cup. Players call it a world
            cup predictor for their cup. It is a free soccer simulation game. It
            is a soccer game with no download. It runs on a laptop, tablet or
            phone. Your save stays on your device.
          </p>
          <p>
            Want the long version? The how-to-play guide explains formations,
            drafting, chemistry and the bracket. The FAQ shows how the football
            simulation works. It shows how penalty shootouts work. Call it
            fantasy soccer. Call it an interactive soccer simulator. Or call it
            the world cup fantasy game. The path is the same.
          </p>
          <p>
            Open the browser soccer game. Draft your dream XI. Simulate the cup.
            Start now. The sooner you start, the sooner your cup lifts a trophy
            you built.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
